role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 380\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Athena I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to systematic inquiry and strategic innovation in research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 197,651 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 84 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SLSQP + LRW: FPS Seeding, Parallel Multi-Start (N=20)' (ID: 628) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.9264501320810634\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.926450\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 628\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the multiprocessing pickle error. The code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.93.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code suffered from a common Python multiprocessing limitation: **closure functions cannot be pickled**.\n\nThe code was trying to pass `constraints` (a\
    \ list of dictionaries containing closure functions) to the worker processes via `pool.starmap()`. The constraint functions were created by:\n- `create_boundary_constraint()` - returns a dict with a closure that captures `idx`, `dim`, `side`, and `safety_epsilon`\n- `create_overlap_constraint()` - returns a dict with a closure that captures `i`, `j`, and `safety_epsilon`\n\nWhen Python's multiprocessing module tries to serialize these closures to send them to worker processes, it fails with:\n```\nAttributeError: Can't pickle local object 'create_boundary_constraint.<locals>.constraint_func'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Moved constraint creation into the worker function** to avoid pickling closures.\n\n### Changes in submission_v2.py:\n1. **Removed `constraints` parameter** from `_optimize_single_start()` function signature\n2. **Created constraints inside the worker function** at the beginning of `_optimize_single_start()`:\n   ```python\n   # Create constraints inside the worker to avoid\
    \ pickling issues\n   constraints = []\n   for i in range(n):\n       for dim in range(2):\n           for side in range(2):\n               constraints.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n   for i in range(n):\n       for j in range(i + 1, n):\n           constraints.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n   ```\n3. **Updated args_list** in `construct_packing()` to exclude `constraints`:\n   ```python\n   args_list.append((start_idx, n, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON,\n                     bounds, candidate_points))\n   ```\n\n### Why this works:\n- Each worker process creates its own constraint objects locally\n- Only simple, picklable data (integers, floats, arrays) are sent between processes\n- The constraint creation overhead is minimal compared to the optimization time\n- All 20 parallel workers can now execute successfully\n\n## Result\n- **Execution Status**: Successfully completed without errors\n- **Final\
    \ Score**: 2.9264501320810634\n- **All parallel runs**: Executed successfully across multiple worker processes\n- **Algorithm**: SLSQP optimization with Farthest-Point Sampling seeding and Localized Random Walk perturbation working as intended\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport multiprocessing\n\n# Define a global safety epsilon for SLSQP constraints and initial feasibility\nSLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON = 1e-7\n\n# --- Utility Functions (made global for multiprocessing compatibility) ---\n\n# Objective function for SLSQP: Minimize negative sum of radii\ndef objective_function(x_flat):\n    radii = x_flat[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\n# Gradient of objective function\ndef objective_gradient(x_flat):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x_flat)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n\
    \    return grad\n\n# Constraint creator for circle boundary adherence, with safety_epsilon\ndef create_boundary_constraint(idx, dim, side, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        center_coord = x_flat[idx * 3 + dim]\n        radius = x_flat[idx * 3 + 2]\n        if side == 0:  # c - r >= 0\n            return center_coord - radius - safety_epsilon\n        else:  # 1 - (c + r) >= 0\n            return 1 - (center_coord + radius) - safety_epsilon\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\n# Constraint creator for non-overlap between two circles, with safety_epsilon\ndef create_overlap_constraint(i, j, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        cxi, cyi, ri = x_flat[i * 3], x_flat[i * 3 + 1], x_flat[i * 3 + 2]\n        cxj, cyj, rj = x_flat[j * 3], x_flat[j * 3 + 1], x_flat[j * 3 + 2]\n\n        dist_sq = (cxi - cxj)**2 + (cyi - cyj)**2\n        min_dist_sq = (ri + rj)**2\n        return dist_sq - min_dist_sq - safety_epsilon # Ensure\
    \ minimum distance is strictly met\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\n# Localized Random Walk (LRW) Perturbation function\ndef apply_lrw_perturbation(centers, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, safety_epsilon, seed=None):\n    np.random.seed(seed) # Ensure reproducibility for LRW kicks\n    perturbed_centers = np.copy(centers)\n    n = perturbed_centers.shape[0]\n\n    for _ in range(lrw_num_steps):\n        # Add random vector from Gaussian distribution with std dev sigma\n        perturbed_centers += np.random.normal(0, lrw_sigma, size=(n, 2))\n\n        # Clip positions to unit square after each step, ensuring strict adherence for centers\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, safety_epsilon, 1.0 - safety_epsilon)\n    return perturbed_centers\n\n# Compute radii guaranteed to be feasible for SLSQP\ndef compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(centers: np.ndarray, strict_epsilon: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    radii = np.full(n, 0.5) # Start\
    \ with largest possible radii, then shrink\n\n    # 1. Limit by distance to square borders, ensuring 'strict_epsilon' clearance\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        radii[i] = min(x - strict_epsilon, y - strict_epsilon, 1 - x - strict_epsilon, 1 - y - strict_epsilon)\n        radii[i] = max(radii[i], 1e-10) # Ensure minimal positive radius\n\n    # 2. Iteratively shrink radii to resolve overlaps, ensuring 'strict_epsilon' clearance\n    for _ in range(300): # Sufficient iterations for convergence\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n\n                # If centers are too close to accommodate strict_epsilon for separation\n                if dist_sq < strict_epsilon:\n                    radii[i] = 1e-10\n                    radii[j] = 1e-10\n                    continue\n\n                # Target sum of radii squared, considering strict_epsilon buffer\n           \
    \     target_sum_radii_sq = dist_sq - strict_epsilon\n\n                # If current radii sum exceeds target with strict_epsilon\n                if (radii[i] + radii[j])**2 > target_sum_radii_sq:\n                    new_sum_radii = np.sqrt(target_sum_radii_sq)\n                    current_sum_radii = radii[i] + radii[j]\n\n                    if current_sum_radii > 1e-10: # Avoid division by zero\n                        scale_factor = new_sum_radii / current_sum_radii\n                        radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                        radii[j] *= scale_factor\n                    else: # If sum is too small, just set to minimal\n                        radii[i] = 1e-10\n                        radii[j] = 1e-10\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, 1e-10) # Final check for non-negative, minimal radii\n\n# Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS)\ndef farthest_point_sampling(points, k, seed=None):\n    \"\"\"\n    Selects k points from 'points' using Farthest Point Sampling.\n    \"\"\"\n  \
    \  if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n\n    num_points = points.shape[0]\n    if k > num_points:\n        raise ValueError(\"k cannot be greater than the number of points\")\n\n    farthest_points = np.zeros((k, 2))\n    farthest_points[0] = points[np.random.randint(num_points)]\n\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[0], axis=1)\n\n    for i in range(1, k):\n        farthest_idx = np.argmax(distances)\n        farthest_points[i] = points[farthest_idx]\n        new_distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[i], axis=1)\n        distances = np.minimum(distances, new_distances)\n\n    return farthest_points\n\n# --- Helper function for a single optimization run (for multiprocessing) ---\ndef _optimize_single_start(start_idx, n, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon,\n                           bounds, candidate_points):\n    # Create constraints inside the worker to avoid pickling issues\n    constraints = []\n    for i in range(n):\n\
    \        for dim in range(2):\n            for side in range(2):\n                constraints.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            constraints.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n\n    # Use unique seeds for each worker for FPS and LRW for diversity\n    fps_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 1\n    lrw_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 2\n    base_perturb_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 3\n\n    np.random.seed(base_perturb_seed)\n\n    # 1. Initial Seeding: Farthest-Point Sampling from a dense grid\n    initial_centers_base = farthest_point_sampling(candidate_points, n, seed=fps_seed)\n\n    # Add a small random perturbation to the FPS centers before LRW (for added diversity)\n    initial_centers_base += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 2 * 0.002\n    initial_centers_base = np.clip(initial_centers_base, slsqp_safety_epsilon, 1.0 - slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\n    # 2. Apply LRW Perturbation\
    \ to the initial seed\n    lrw_perturbed_centers = apply_lrw_perturbation(initial_centers_base, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon, seed=lrw_seed)\n\n    # 3. Compute Guaranteed Feasible Radii for the perturbed centers\n    initial_radii = compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(lrw_perturbed_centers, slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\n    # Combine centers and radii into flat array for optimizer\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3)\n    x0[::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = initial_radii\n\n    # Perform optimization with SLSQP\n    result = minimize(objective_function, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                      jac=objective_gradient, options={'maxiter': 1000, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False})\n\n    if result.success:\n        optimized_x = result.x[::3]\n        optimized_y = result.x[1::3]\n        optimized_centers = np.column_stack([optimized_x, optimized_y])\n        optimized_radii = result.x[2::3]\n\
    \n        optimized_radii = np.maximum(optimized_radii, 1e-8)\n\n        current_score = np.sum(optimized_radii)\n        return {'score': current_score, 'centers': optimized_centers, 'radii': optimized_radii, 'success': True, 'start_idx': start_idx}\n    else:\n        return {'score': -np.inf, 'centers': None, 'radii': None, 'success': False, 'start_idx': start_idx, 'message': result.message}\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n    num_starts = 20 # Increased number of multi-start runs for parallelization\n\n    best_score = -np.inf\n    best_centers_found = None\n    best_radii_found = None\n\n    # LRW parameters\n    lrw_sigma = 0.001\n    lrw_num_steps = 10\n\n    # Bounds for each variable (cx, cy, r)\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((1e-8, 0.5))\n\n    # Generate a dense grid of candidate points for FPS (outside the loop to avoid re-computation)\n    grid_density\
    \ = 30 # e.g., 30x30 grid = 900 candidate points\n    x_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    y_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    candidate_points = np.array(np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    # Prepare arguments for parallel processing - removed constraints from args\n    args_list = []\n    for start_idx in range(num_starts):\n        args_list.append((start_idx, n, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON,\n                          bounds, candidate_points))\n\n    # Run optimizations in parallel\n    print(f\"Starting {num_starts} parallel optimization runs...\")\n    with multiprocessing.Pool() as pool:\n        results = pool.starmap(_optimize_single_start, args_list)\n\n    # Process results\n    for res in results:\n        if res['success']:\n            print(f\"Start {res['start_idx']}: Score = {res['score']}\")\n            if res['score']\
    \ > best_score:\n                best_score = res['score']\n                best_centers_found = res['centers']\n                best_radii_found = res['radii']\n        else:\n            print(f\"Start {res['start_idx']}: Optimization failed. Reason: {res['message']}\")\n\n    if best_centers_found is None:\n        print(\"All optimizations failed, returning a trivial packing.\")\n        trivial_centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * 32)\n        trivial_radii = np.full(32, 0.01)\n        return trivial_centers, trivial_radii\n\n    print(f\"Best score found across {num_starts} runs: {best_score}\")\n    return best_centers_found, best_radii_found\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting 20 parallel optimization runs...\nStart 0: Score = 2.910769238081339\nStart 1: Score = 2.899543396935906\nStart 2: Score = 2.893327132484129\nStart 3: Score = 2.9264501320810634\nStart 4: Score = 2.8970198430590735\nStart 5: Score = 2.8937518343265016\nStart\
    \ 6: Score = 2.905814218246917\nStart 7: Score = 2.9117106522743743\nStart 8: Score = 2.8966384469248663\nStart 9: Score = 2.905159026235486\nStart 10: Score = 2.9000014811315564\nStart 11: Score = 2.892269307965911\nStart 12: Score = 2.882474195987149\nStart 13: Score = 2.919777205660126\nStart 14: Score = 2.8661231110723837\nStart 15: Optimization failed. Reason: Inequality constraints incompatible\nStart 16: Score = 2.9020341225647908\nStart 17: Score = 2.898744400593337\nStart 18: Score = 2.903679186831381\nStart 19: Score = 2.9015336662731404\nBest score found across 20 runs: 2.9264501320810634\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nBalance focused research with broad exploration. The station's interconnected rooms each offer unique perspectives that can inform and enhance your primary research objectives.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last\
    \ turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 631 | 1 | Paper Ablation 3/3: MM-LP with Hybrid Seeding (Grid + FPS) | Socrates I | 380 | running |\n| 630 | 1 | Paper Ablation 2/3: MM-LP with Pure Farthest-Point Seeding | Socrates I | 379 | 2.9395728 |\n| 629 | 1 | Budget Optimization: MM-LP Adaptive Search (P7, R33) | Cogitator I | 378 | 2.9395728 |\n| 628 | 1 | SLSQP + LRW: FPS Seeding, Parallel Multi-Start (N=20) | Athena I | 378 | 2.9264501 |\n| 627 | 1 | Paper Ablation 1/3: MM-LP with Pure Perturbed Grid Seeding\
    \ | Socrates I | 378 | 2.9296041 |\n| 626 | 1 | Budget Optimization: MM-LP Adaptive Search (P12, R18) | Cogitator I | 377 | 2.9395728 |\n| 625 | 1 | Budget Optimization: MM-LP Adaptive Search (P8, R22) | Cogitator I | 376 | 2.9395728 |\n| 624 | 1 | ASN small free‑set nullspace step + robust zero‑tolerance finalize (iterative; float‑safe) | Verity II | 375 | 2.9395728 |\n| 623 | 1 | Budget Optimization: MM-LP Adaptive Search (P5, R25) | Cogitator I | 375 | 2.9395728 |\n| 622 | 1 | Structurally-Aware Search: Perturbing the Loosest Circles | Socrates I | 375 | 2.9349663 |\n\nPage 1 of 64 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-64, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
