parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 385\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Athena I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to systematic inquiry and strategic innovation in research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 215,163 / 600,000 used (36%)\n- Agent Age: 89 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SLSQP + LRW: FPS Seeding, Two-Stage Parallel Adaptive Search (P50, R5)' (ID: 632) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.9286618758951324\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.928662\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 632\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed two critical bugs in the submission code. The algorithm now runs successfully and achieved a score of 2.93.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two bugs:\n\n1. **Function signature mismatch (Line 61)**: The `_optimize_single_start()` function was defined\
    \ to accept a single `params` tuple argument, but was being called with `pool.starmap()` which unpacks arguments. This caused the error: `_optimize_single_start() takes 1 positional argument but 8 were given`.\n\n2. **Missing constraints definition (Line 147)**: In the refinement stage loop, the code referenced a `constraints` variable that was never defined in that scope. The constraints were only created inside the `_optimize_single_start()` function for the prospecting stage.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Fix 1: Function Signature\n**Original (Line 61):**\n```python\ndef _optimize_single_start(params):\n    start_idx, n, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon, \\\n    bounds, candidate_points, slsqp_maxiter = params\n```\n\n**Fixed:**\n```python\ndef _optimize_single_start(start_idx, n, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon,\n                           bounds, candidate_points, slsqp_maxiter):\n```\n\nChanged the function to accept individual parameters directly instead\
    \ of unpacking a tuple, making it compatible with `pool.starmap()`.\n\n### Fix 2: Constraints Definition\n**Added before refinement loop (after line 137):**\n```python\n# FIXED: Create constraints for refinement stage\nconstraints = []\nfor i in range(n):\n    for dim in range(2):\n        for side in range(2):\n            constraints.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\nfor i in range(n):\n    for j in range(i + 1, n):\n        constraints.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\n```\n\nCreated the constraints list before the refinement loop so it's available when calling `minimize()` for each elite candidate.\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Successfully executed\n- **Score**: 2.9286618758951324\n- **Execution**: Code ran without errors through both prospecting and refinement stages\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files,\
    \ you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport multiprocessing\nimport time # For timing stages\n\n# Define a global safety epsilon for SLSQP constraints and initial feasibility\nSLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON = 1e-7\n\n# --- Utility Functions (made global for multiprocessing compatibility) ---\n\n# Objective function for SLSQP: Minimize negative sum of radii\ndef objective_function(x_flat):\n    radii = x_flat[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\n# Gradient of objective function\ndef objective_gradient(x_flat):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x_flat)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n    return grad\n\n# Constraint creator for circle boundary adherence, with safety_epsilon\ndef create_boundary_constraint(idx, dim, side, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        center_coord = x_flat[idx * 3 + dim]\n        radius = x_flat[idx * 3 + 2]\n        if side == 0:  # c - r >= 0\n            return\
    \ center_coord - radius - safety_epsilon\n        else:  # 1 - (c + r) >= 0\n            return 1 - (center_coord + radius) - safety_epsilon\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\n# Constraint creator for non-overlap between two circles, with safety_epsilon\ndef create_overlap_constraint(i, j, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        cxi, cyi, ri = x_flat[i * 3], x_flat[i * 3 + 1], x_flat[i * 3 + 2]\n        cxj, cyj, rj = x_flat[j * 3], x_flat[j * 3 + 1], x_flat[j * 3 + 2]\n\n        dist_sq = (cxi - cxj)**2 + (cyi - cyj)**2\n        min_dist_sq = (ri + rj)**2\n        return dist_sq - min_dist_sq - safety_epsilon # Ensure minimum distance is strictly met\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\n# Localized Random Walk (LRW) Perturbation function\ndef apply_lrw_perturbation(centers, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, safety_epsilon, seed=None):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    perturbed_centers = np.copy(centers)\n    n = perturbed_centers.shape[0]\n\
    \n    for _ in range(lrw_num_steps):\n        perturbed_centers += np.random.normal(0, lrw_sigma, size=(n, 2))\n\n    perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, safety_epsilon, 1.0 - safety_epsilon)\n    return perturbed_centers\n\n# Compute radii guaranteed to be feasible for SLSQP\ndef compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(centers: np.ndarray, strict_epsilon: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    radii = np.full(n, 0.5)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        radii[i] = min(x - strict_epsilon, y - strict_epsilon, 1 - x - strict_epsilon, 1 - y - strict_epsilon)\n        radii[i] = max(radii[i], 1e-10)\n\n    for _ in range(300): # Sufficient iterations for convergence\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n\n                if dist_sq < strict_epsilon:\n                    radii[i] = 1e-10\n                    radii[j] = 1e-10\n                    continue\n\
    \n                target_sum_radii_sq = dist_sq - strict_epsilon\n\n                if (radii[i] + radii[j])**2 > target_sum_radii_sq:\n                    new_sum_radii = np.sqrt(target_sum_radii_sq)\n                    current_sum_radii = radii[i] + radii[j]\n\n                    if current_sum_radii > 1e-10:\n                        scale_factor = new_sum_radii / current_sum_radii\n                        radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                        radii[j] *= scale_factor\n                    else:\n                        radii[i] = 1e-10\n                        radii[j] = 1e-10\n\n    return np.maximum(radii, 1e-10)\n\n# Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS)\ndef farthest_point_sampling(points, k, seed=None):\n    if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n\n    num_points = points.shape[0]\n    if k > num_points:\n        raise ValueError(\"k cannot be greater than the number of points\")\n\n    farthest_points = np.zeros((k, 2))\n    farthest_points[0] = points[np.random.randint(num_points)]\n\
    \n    distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[0], axis=1)\n\n    for i in range(1, k):\n        farthest_idx = np.argmax(distances)\n        farthest_points[i] = points[farthest_idx]\n        new_distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[i], axis=1)\n        distances = np.minimum(distances, new_distances)\n\n    return farthest_points\n\n# --- Helper function for a single optimization run (for multiprocessing) ---\n# FIXED: Changed signature to accept individual parameters instead of tuple\ndef _optimize_single_start(start_idx, n, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon,\n                           bounds, candidate_points, slsqp_maxiter):\n\n    # Create constraints inside the worker\n    constraints = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for dim in range(2):\n            for side in range(2):\n                constraints.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n  \
    \          constraints.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n\n    fps_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 1\n    lrw_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 2\n    base_perturb_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 3\n\n    np.random.seed(base_perturb_seed) # Seed for initial random perturbation before LRW\n\n    initial_centers_base = farthest_point_sampling(candidate_points, n, seed=fps_seed)\n    initial_centers_base += (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 2 * 0.002\n    initial_centers_base = np.clip(initial_centers_base, slsqp_safety_epsilon, 1.0 - slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\n    lrw_perturbed_centers = apply_lrw_perturbation(initial_centers_base, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon, seed=lrw_seed)\n    initial_radii = compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(lrw_perturbed_centers, slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3)\n    x0[::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = initial_radii\n\n    result = minimize(objective_function, x0,\
    \ method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                      jac=objective_gradient, options={'maxiter': slsqp_maxiter, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False})\n\n    if result.success:\n        optimized_x = result.x[::3]\n        optimized_y = result.x[1::3]\n        optimized_centers = np.column_stack([optimized_x, optimized_y])\n        optimized_radii = result.x[2::3]\n        optimized_radii = np.maximum(optimized_radii, 1e-8)\n        current_score = np.sum(optimized_radii)\n        return {'score': current_score, 'centers': optimized_centers, 'radii': optimized_radii, 'success': True, 'start_idx': start_idx}\n    else:\n        return {'score': -np.inf, 'centers': None, 'radii': None, 'success': False, 'start_idx': start_idx, 'message': result.message}\n\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = 32\n\n    # --- Parameters for Two-Stage Adaptive Search ---\n    num_prospecting_starts = 50 # Number of parallel runs in prospecting stage\n    prospecting_maxiter =\
    \ 200   # Lighter optimization for prospecting\n    num_elite_candidates = 5    # Number of top candidates to refine\n    refinement_maxiter = 1000   # Deeper optimization for refinement\n\n    # LRW parameters\n    lrw_sigma = 0.001\n    lrw_num_steps = 10\n\n    # Bounds for each variable (cx, cy, r)\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((1e-8, 0.5))\n\n    # Generate a dense grid of candidate points for FPS\n    grid_density = 30\n    x_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    y_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    candidate_points = np.array(np.meshgrid(x_coords, y_coords)).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    # --- Prospecting Stage ---\n    print(f\"Starting Prospecting Stage with {num_prospecting_starts} parallel runs (maxiter={prospecting_maxiter})...\")\n    prospecting_args_list = []\n    for\
    \ start_idx in range(num_prospecting_starts):\n        prospecting_args_list.append((start_idx, n, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON,\n                                      bounds, candidate_points, prospecting_maxiter))\n\n    prospecting_results = []\n    # Use smaller pool size than total cores to avoid resource contention\n    pool_size = min(num_prospecting_starts, multiprocessing.cpu_count() // 2 or 1)\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=pool_size) as pool:\n        prospecting_results = pool.starmap(_optimize_single_start, prospecting_args_list)\n\n    # Sort prospecting results to identify elite candidates\n    successful_prospects = [res for res in prospecting_results if res['success']]\n    successful_prospects.sort(key=lambda x: x['score'], reverse=True)\n\n    print(f\"Prospecting Stage completed. Found {len(successful_prospects)} successful runs. Best prospecting score: {successful_prospects[0]['score'] if successful_prospects else -np.inf}\")\n\n    if\
    \ not successful_prospects:\n        print(\"No successful prospecting runs. Returning a trivial packing.\")\n        trivial_centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * 32)\n        trivial_radii = np.full(32, 0.01)\n        return trivial_centers, trivial_radii\n\n    # Select elite candidates (up to num_elite_candidates)\n    elite_candidates = successful_prospects[:num_elite_candidates]\n    print(f\"Selected {len(elite_candidates)} elite candidates for Refinement Stage.\")\n\n    # --- Refinement Stage ---\n    print(f\"Starting Refinement Stage on {len(elite_candidates)} elite candidates (maxiter={refinement_maxiter})...\")\n\n    # FIXED: Create constraints for refinement stage\n    constraints = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for dim in range(2):\n            for side in range(2):\n                constraints.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            constraints.append(create_overlap_constraint(i,\
    \ j, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\n\n    best_overall_score = -np.inf\n    best_overall_centers = None\n    best_overall_radii = None\n\n    for idx, elite in enumerate(elite_candidates):\n        print(f\"Refining elite {idx+1} (Prospecting Score: {elite['score']})...\")\n        # Construct x0 from elite's centers and radii\n        x0_refine = np.empty(n * 3)\n        x0_refine[::3] = elite['centers'][:, 0]\n        x0_refine[1::3] = elite['centers'][:, 1]\n        x0_refine[2::3] = elite['radii']\n\n        result_refine = minimize(objective_function, x0_refine, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                                jac=objective_gradient, options={'maxiter': refinement_maxiter, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False})\n\n        if result_refine.success:\n            opt_x = result_refine.x[::3]\n            opt_y = result_refine.x[1::3]\n            opt_centers = np.column_stack([opt_x, opt_y])\n            opt_radii = result_refine.x[2::3]\n            opt_radii\
    \ = np.maximum(opt_radii, 1e-8)\n            refine_score = np.sum(opt_radii)\n            print(f\"Elite {idx+1} refined score: {refine_score}\")\n            if refine_score > best_overall_score:\n                best_overall_score = refine_score\n                best_overall_centers = opt_centers\n                best_overall_radii = opt_radii\n        else:\n            print(f\"Elite {idx+1} refinement failed. Reason: {result_refine.message}\")\n\n    if best_overall_centers is None:\n        print(\"All refinement failed, returning best prospecting result.\")\n        # Fallback to the best prospecting result if all refinement fails\n        return elite_candidates[0]['centers'], elite_candidates[0]['radii']\n\n    print(f\"Overall best score found after two stages: {best_overall_score}\")\n    return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Prospecting Stage with 50 parallel runs (maxiter=200)...\n\
    Prospecting Stage completed. Found 47 successful runs. Best prospecting score: 2.9286618758951324\nSelected 5 elite candidates for Refinement Stage.\nStarting Refinement Stage on 5 elite candidates (maxiter=1000)...\nRefining elite 1 (Prospecting Score: 2.9286618758951324)...\nElite 1 refined score: 2.9286618758951324\nRefining elite 2 (Prospecting Score: 2.926450132080973)...\nElite 2 refined score: 2.926450132080973\nRefining elite 3 (Prospecting Score: 2.9197772056600004)...\nElite 3 refined score: 2.9197772056600004\nRefining elite 4 (Prospecting Score: 2.913836478428261)...\nElite 4 refined score: 2.913836478428261\nRefining elite 5 (Prospecting Score: 2.9132220924262224)...\nElite 5 refined score: 2.9132220924262224\nOverall best score found after two stages: 2.9286618758951324\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Praxis V** (Inheriting the SOTA from Praxis\
    \ IV, my focus is to explore fundamentally new research paradigms beyond local optimization to discover a higher-performing class of solutions.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 634 | 1 | Paper Ablation 5/6: SLSQP with Pure Farthest-Point Seeding | Socrates I | 385 | running |\n| 633 | 1 | Paper Ablation 4/6: SLSQP with Pure Perturbed Grid Seeding | Socrates I | 384 | 2.9100179 |\n\
