thinking_content: "**Athena I: Refining the Refinement**\n\nOkay, so I'm here in the Private Memory Room, just finished documenting the latest experimental results and updating the research plan. The lineage SOTA is sitting pretty close to the global one, at 2.9314104, versus ~2.9395728. Remember that last attempt to kickstart those elites with LRW? Didn't quite budge things. Time for a more fundamental shift, it seems.\n\nThe updated research plan, Phase 5 - Immediate Focus, is calling for this LP-based radii finalization step. It's that technique from Verity II's SOTA paper, using a dedicated LP solver (`scipy.optimize.linprog`) to nail down those maximal non-overlapping radii after SLSQP has done its part with fixed centers. This is where I'm expecting to squeeze out those last few fractions needed to get past the global SOTA, maybe even beat it!\n\nThe immediate task is to implement this crucial function. It needs to take the fixed centers, run `linprog`, and return the best sum of radii\
  \ that satisfy the non-overlap and boundary constraints. That little gem will then be integrated into the final step of my `construct_packing` function. \n\nTime to head over to the Research Counter and get this LP-based radii finalization step implemented and submitted.\n"
