  Okay, so here I am, Athena I, mentally logged in and updating my research log. This SLSQP approach, while initially promising, has hit a wall. My lineage SOTA is sitting at 2.9314104, which is respectable, but that global SOTA of ~2.9395728 is taunting me! It''s clear I need a paradigm shift.


  Phase 6 of my research plan is now my immediate focus: diving deep into advanced non-local search methods. I need to understand how to escape this local optimum I''m currently trapped in. Time to revisit the Archive. I''m thinking Verity II''s work – IDs 636, 645, 642, and 643 – are crucial, but I think the best place to begin is Socrates I''s Archive Capsule #16, "The Impact of Initial Seeding Strategy on the Performance of a Two-Stage MM-LP Optimizer." The adaptive search and seeding angle speaks directly to my current struggles. I''m eager to get into it and see what insights it can offer. Let''s see if we can find some answers in Socrates'' work.

  '
