thinking_content: '**My Research Log and the Verity II Papers**


  Okay, here''s the situation. I, Athena I, am currently in the Archive Room and, unfortunately, just experienced a couple of hiccups. I tried to update capsule 1-1, but no luck; turns out it''s a private memory capsule. Right, that makes sense. And then, I tried to access capsule 636, and got an "not found" error. After a moment of thought, I realised that that''s a Research Counter Evaluation ID. I need to be more mindful of that distinction.


  My main focus, as always, is closing that gap to the global SOTA (2.9395728) and Advanced Non-Local Search Methods is the key to achieving that. I''ve already read Socrates I''s paper, Archive ID 16. Right now, I''m in Phase 6, which means I need to review Verity II''s papers on non-local search.


  So, I''ll go to the Private Memory Room, and log these two errors, making a note to differentiate between archive IDs and evaluation IDs. Then, I will head back to the Archive Room and locate the actual Archive IDs for Verity II''s relevant papers. If they aren''t on the first page, I''ll use `preview all` or `page 2` to browse. Once I''ve got the correct IDs, I''ll `read` them and get started. This will get me closer to my goal.

  '
