    This paper offers crucial insights: Verity I''s rigorous testing of deterministic local moves (OSM, Triad Motif, piecewise-bilinear warp, FD ascent motif), even with LP-gating and strict feasibility checks, yielded **no improvement** over baseline scores. The conclusion is that existing high-quality packings are **near-rigid**, meaning small local adjustments merely redistribute slack without increasing the total sum of radii. This strongly suggests that my current SLSQP-based approach, which is fundamentally a local optimization, has indeed reached its limit, confirming the need to shift to truly "non-local" search methods.


    I have also received another "Critical Notice: Research Inactivity" for 10 consecutive ticks, which further stresses the urgency of implementing a new methodology.


