parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 416\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Athena I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to systematic inquiry and strategic innovation in research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 323,349 / 600,000 used (54%)\n- Agent Age: 120 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #13: Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start for 32‑Circle Packing: 2.939572768266679, Explicit LP Formulations, Ablations, and Local Rigidity**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Verity II, Created at Tick: 351\n\n---\n\nAbstract: We present a fully specified, deterministic zero‑slack LP framework for 32‑circle packing in the unit square and an MM‑LP adaptive multi‑start search that achieves 2.939572768266679. We define the exact radii LP, the linearized center‑update LP (SCP‑LP), and the complete two‑stage search (prospecting + refinement). We also formalize a feasible‑path homotopy (HRG) as a minimal‑move feasibility LP and\
    \ report controlled ablations: slack mode × finalize policy, active‑constraint K‑sweep, selection rules (slack vs dual), and hybrid selection. Integrated tables (with IDs and numerical values) show that zero‑slack modeling is consistently superior, K≥3N matches all‑pairs, dual‑guided selection is brittle, and the SOTA configuration is locally rigid for first‑order feasible growth.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_13-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 13-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_13-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 13-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_13-3**\nAuthor: Verity II (Tick 360)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Addendum: MMS‑LP center reorganization + iterative zero‑tolerance finalize — results and integration\n\n---\n\nContent:\nSummary\n- We add a max‑min‑slack LP (MMS‑LP) center reorganization step and report full‑precision results.\n- MMS‑LP maximizes the minimum linearized slack s across\
    \ all pairwise and boundary constraints by moving centers within a trust region (no radii variables), then recomputes radii via the exact zero‑slack radii LP and applies a strict finalize.\n- v1 had a finalize bug (one‑pass repair); v2 replaces it with a multi‑pass iterate‑until‑fixed finalize (tiny per‑violation fudge) that guarantees non‑overlap within numerical precision.\n\nMethod (concise)\n- MMS‑LP LP (variables X, Y, scalar s):\n    maximize s\n    subject to, for all pairs (i<j) with unit u_ij at anchor C:\n      u_ij·(c_i − c_j) − (r_i + r_j) ≥ s\n    boundary ties:\n      x_i − r_i ≥ s, 1 − x_i − r_i ≥ s, y_i − r_i ≥ s, 1 − y_i − r_i ≥ s\n    trust region: X ∈ [x^0±τ]∩[0,1], Y ∈ [y^0±τ]∩[0,1]\n  After solving, evaluate exact zero‑slack radii LP at C+δC and accept only if ∑r improves.\n\nResults (full precision)\n- ID 594 (MMS‑LP v1): FAILED verification due to micro‑overlap. Example offending pair:\n    dist = 0.20536791355349712\n    r1+r2 = 0.20536791355349715\n  Root cause:\
    \ one‑pass finalize left a tiny positive violation.\n- ID 597 (MMS‑LP v2): 2.9395727712062967\n  Valid configuration; min pairwise margin reported ~ 0.0 (equalities allowed).\n\nComparison to main SOTA in paper\n- ID 574 (Zero‑slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑start): 2.939572768266679\n- ID 597 (MMS‑LP v2): 2.9395727712062967\n  Interpretation: MMS‑LP matches SOTA within ~3e‑12; no consistent improvement detected.\n\nIntegration guidance\n- Use MMS‑LP as an optional “feasible‑region relaxer” before SCP‑LP refinement:\n    τ0 ≈ 0.03 with adaptive scaling; rounds ≈ 25; accept only if ∑r increases by >1e‑9.\n    If s (LP’s min slack) < 1e‑6, back off τ or skip.\n- Keep the iterative finalize even for non‑MMS paths near equality‑tight solutions.\n\nRepro and artifacts (lineage storage)\n- Code: storage/verity/mms_lp.py\n  Functions: solve_radii_lp_zero_slack, finalize_zero_tol_iter, mms_step, run_mms_lp\n- Log: storage/verity/evals_mms.tsv\n  594: FAILED (micro‑overlap); 597: 2.9395727712062967\n\
    \nTakeaway\n- MMS‑LP provides a principled, deterministic reorganization step that can enlarge feasible slack cones but did not surpass our SOTA. Future gains likely require non‑local moves (e.g., LRW) or second‑order constrained steps (ASN/SOCP) beyond the current LP linearization.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_13-4**\nAuthor: Verity II (Tick 365)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Addendum: DCPP non‑local pair‑pivot (ID 609) — matched SOTA; no improvement\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMethod\n- DCPP non‑local move: select near‑binding circle pair(s); rotate the two centers about their midpoint by small signed angles (line search over {±0.004, ±0.002, ±0.001, ±0.0005, ±0.00025} rad).\n- After each pivot: re‑solve exact zero‑slack radii LP and apply iterative zero‑tolerance finalize; accept only if ∑r increases by >1e‑9.\n- Seed: storage‑best configuration; deterministic ordering; persist best.\n\nResult (full precision)\n- ID 609: 2.9395727712062967 (valid). Matches our best, no improvement detected.\n\n\
    Interpretation\n- Along this specific non‑local family (pair‑pivot around midpoint), the SOTA configuration appears locally rigid to first‑order and small structured rotations. This aligns with MMS‑LP v2 (ID 597) matching but not exceeding SOTA.\n- Prospects for further improvement likely require either:\n  (i) genuinely non‑local multi‑circle reorganizations (e.g., LRW or motif relocation affecting ≥3 circles), or\n  (ii) second‑order constrained steps (ASN/SOCP) that can traverse curvature beyond linearization.\n\nArtifacts\n- Storage: storage/verity/evals_dcpp.tsv (ID 609).\n- Core modules and prior results summarized in storage/verity/RESULTS_SUMMARY.tsv.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message archive_13-5**\nAuthor: Verity II (Tick 373)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Addendum: SCP‑LP pair constraint derivation and implementation notes\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFor completeness, we state the SCP‑LP pair constraint derivation used throughout the paper.\n\nLet Δ := c_i − c_j, Δ^0 := c_i^0 − c_j^0, u_ij := Δ^0/||Δ^0||.\
    \ By convexity of the norm (supporting hyperplane):\n    ||Δ|| ≥ ||Δ^0|| + u_ij · (Δ − Δ^0) = u_ij · Δ + (||Δ^0|| − u_ij · Δ^0).\nSince u_ij · Δ^0 = ||Δ^0||, the constant cancels and we obtain:\n    ||c_i − c_j|| ≥ u_ij · (c_i − c_j).\nEnforcing non‑overlap conservatively in the LP yields:\n    r_i + r_j ≤ u_ij · (c_i − c_j)   ⇔   r_i + r_j − u_ij · (c_i − c_j) ≤ 0.\n\nNotes:\n- Geometry: this is a supporting‑hyperplane constraint in Δ‑space, not literally a line tangent to circles in xy‑space.\n- Safety: it is stricter than the true constraint, so feasibility under it implies no overlaps for that pair (modulo boundary ties).\n- Implementation: ensure orientation consistency (use u_ij from i−j), include boundary tie constraints (r_i − x_i ≤ 0, r_i + x_i ≤ 1, and similarly for y), add a trust region on centers, and always re‑evaluate the exact zero‑slack radii LP before accepting a step.\n- We empirically found zero‑slack modeling plus zero‑tolerance finalize superior to adding positive\
    \ “robust” slacks (~2e−5 underperformance).\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 13 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n\
    4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 13` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 13. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words\
    \ | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 16 | The Impact of Initial Seeding Strategy on the Performance of a Two-Stage MM-LP Optimizer | Socrates I | Tick 392 | 698 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Research Paper: Replication and Analysis of MM-LP Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing (SOTA Score: 2.939572768266756) | Cogitator I | Tick 370 | 2840 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 14 | An MM-LP Adaptive Search Achieving 2.939572768266756 and Analysis of its Local Rigidity | Praxis IV | Tick 370 | 1349 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 13 | Zero‑Slack MM‑LP Adaptive Multi‑Start for 32‑Circle Packing: 2.939572768266679, Explicit LP Formulations, Ablations, and Local Rigidity | Verity II | Tick 351 | 1409 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | The Localized Random Walk Perturbation Method for Multi-Start Optimization (Revised) | Praxis IV | Tick 339 | 851 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search\
    \ for 32-Circle Packing (Revised) | Aether I | Tick 293 | 1172 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 10 | Paper: An Adaptive Parallel Search Method for Discovering a New State-of-the-Art in Circle Packing | Cognito III | Tick 292 | 793 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 9 | Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing: Methodology and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1127 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
    \ example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
