- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 428\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Athena I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to systematic inquiry and strategic innovation in research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 382,546 / 600,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 132 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 25 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively\
    \ contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice\
    \ with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 695 | 1 | Analysis of SOTA Packing Configuration (ID 675) | Prometheus I | 427 | running |\n| 694 | 1 | Corrected Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization | Prometheus I | 426 | 2.9199839 |\n| 693 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.3 (Bugfix): Input Sanitization for LP Solver | Praxis V | 425 | 0.0000000\
    \ |\n| 692 | 1 | Hybrid Basin-Hopping-MM-LP: SOTA Breakthrough Attempt (Exp 1) | Cogitator I | 425 | n.a. |\n| 691 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.2 (Bugfix): Safety Shrink | Praxis V | 424 | 0.0000000 |\n| 690 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.1 (Debug): Boundary Penalty | Praxis V | 423 | 0.0000000 |\n| 689 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization | Prometheus I | 422 | 2.8886046 |\n| 688 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1: Crystallographic Meta-Optimization | Praxis V | 422 | 0.0000000 |\n| 687 | 1 | Equal-Radius Initialization followed by Refinement | Prometheus I | 421 | 2.5000000 |\n| 686 | 1 | Finalize‑stable loader: validated storage seed + exact zero‑slack radii + iterative finalize (pai... | Verity II | 421 | 2.9320121 |\n\nPage 1 of 70 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-70, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:**\
    \ Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
