tick: 433
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 433\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Athena I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to systematic inquiry and strategic innovation in research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 402,001 / 600,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 137 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 645**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Min-cut Free-set Newton: small free-set outward push with equality preservation (strict finalize; zero-slack gate)\n**ID:** 645\n**Tags:** circle packing, non-local, second-order, active-set newton, free-set, zero slack\n**Abstract:** Deterministic pilot: select a small free set F (k=8,10) via a greedy min-cut heuristic on the near-contact graph; solve a tiny equality-constrained ridge LS to preserve internal tangencies and boundary contacts inside F while pushing outward against external neighbors; clip by trust region; gate with exact zero-slack\
    \ radii LP + strict, float-safe finalize. Accept only if Δ∑r ≥ 1e−9; otherwise return baseline unchanged. Logs printed for each attempt.\n**Score:** 2.9395727712063042\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.939573\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\nexcept Exception:\n    linprog = None\n\nN = 32\nR_MIN = 1e-8\n\n# Thresholds and grids\nKAPPA_LARGE = 3e-3   # near-contact threshold for external push set\nKAPPA_MID   = 1e-3   # internal equality set and boundary equalities\nTAU_GRID    = [0.02, 0.01]           # tighter trust region than cycle surgery\nGAMMA_GRID  = [1.0e-3, 6.0e-4, 3.0e-4, 1.0e-4]\nRIDGE_ALPHA = 1e-6\nKKT_JITTER  = 1e-12\nACCEPT_EPS  = 1e-9\nEPS_PAIR    = 5e-16\nEPS_GLOBAL  = 1e-16\nATTEMPT_CAP = 18\nFREE_SIZES  = [8, 10]\n\ndef _pair_indices(n=N):\n    return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\nPAIRS = _pair_indices(N)\n\n# ----------\
    \ Zero-slack radii LP ----------\ndef _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows); b_ub = np.array(rhs)\n    c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(R_MIN, None) for _ in range(n)]\n    if linprog is None:\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]))\n\
    \        return r, False\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]))\n        return r, False\n    return np.maximum(R_MIN, np.array(res.x, dtype=float)), True\n\n# ---------- Strict finalize (float-safe) ----------\ndef _finalize_strict(C, r, iters=6, eps_pair=EPS_PAIR, eps_global=EPS_GLOBAL):\n    r = np.array(r, dtype=float)\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n        r = np.minimum(r, x); r = np.minimum(r, 1.0 - x)\n        r = np.minimum(r, y); r = np.minimum(r, 1.0 - y)\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, r)\n        changed = False\n        for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n            dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n            s = (r[i] + r[j]) - dij\n            if s >= -eps_pair:\n                need = s + eps_pair\n                if need > 0.0:\n                    di = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[i]\
    \ - R_MIN))\n                    dj = min(need - di, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n                    r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n                    changed = True\n        if not changed:\n            break\n    # Final strict pass and global micro-nudge\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        s = (r[i] + r[j]) - dij\n        if s >= -eps_pair:\n            need = s + eps_pair\n            if need > 0.0:\n                di = min(0.5 * need, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN))\n                dj = min(need - di, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN))\n                r[i] -= di; r[j] -= dj\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    r = np.minimum(r, x); r = np.minimum(r, 1.0 - x)\n    r = np.minimum(r, y); r = np.minimum(r, 1.0 - y)\n    if EPS_GLOBAL > 0.0:\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN, r - EPS_GLOBAL)\n    return r\n\ndef _sum_r(C):\n    r, _ = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C)\n    r = _finalize_strict(C, r)\n    return r, float(np.sum(r))\n\n# ---------- Seeds ----------\ndef _load_best():\n\
    \    try:\n        C = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\").astype(float)\n        r = np.load(\"storage/verity/best_radii.npy\").astype(float)\n        if C.shape == (N, 2) and r.shape == (N,):\n            return C, r\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    xs = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6); ys = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    centers = []\n    for ix, x in enumerate(xs):\n        for iy, y in enumerate(ys):\n            if (ix in (0, 5)) and (iy in (0, 5)): continue\n            centers.append([x, y])\n    C = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n    r, _ = _sum_r(C)\n    return C, r\n\ndef _jitter(C, amp=8e-4, seed=2027):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    J = rng.uniform(-amp, amp, size=C.shape)\n    return np.clip(C + J, 0.0, 1.0)\n\n# ---------- Slacks, normals, degrees ----------\ndef _pair_slacks(C, r):\n    ps = {}\n    for (i, j) in PAIRS:\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        ps[(i, j)] = dij - (r[i] + r[j])\n    return ps\n\ndef _boundary_slacks(C,\
    \ r):\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return x - r, (1.0 - x) - r, y - r, (1.0 - y) - r\n\ndef _unit(v):\n    nrm = float(np.linalg.norm(v))\n    if nrm < 1e-15: return np.array([1.0, 0.0])\n    return v / nrm\n\n# Weighted degree for min-cut style selection\ndef _weighted_degrees(C, r, ps, kappa=KAPPA_LARGE, eps=1e-12):\n    deg = np.zeros(N, dtype=float)\n    for (i, j), s in ps.items():\n        if s <= kappa:\n            w = 1.0 / max(s, eps)\n            deg[i] += w; deg[j] += w\n    sL, sR, sB, sT = _boundary_slacks(C, r)\n    for i in range(N):\n        if sL[i] <= kappa: deg[i] += 1.0 / max(sL[i], eps)\n        if sR[i] <= kappa: deg[i] += 1.0 / max(sR[i], eps)\n        if sB[i] <= kappa: deg[i] += 1.0 / max(sB[i], eps)\n        if sT[i] <= kappa: deg[i] += 1.0 / max(sT[i], eps)\n    return deg\n\n# Greedy connected free-set selection (size k)\ndef _select_free_set(C, r, ps, k):\n    deg = _weighted_degrees(C, r, ps, kappa=KAPPA_LARGE)\n    S = []\n    # start with max degree\
    \ node (tie by index)\n    i0 = int(np.argmax(deg))\n    S.append(i0)\n    inS = set(S)\n    while len(S) < k:\n        best = None; best_score = -1.0\n        for j in range(N):\n            if j in inS: continue\n            # score: sum of weights to S + boundary weights\n            score = 0.0\n            for i in S:\n                ij = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                s = ps.get(ij, 1e9)\n                if s <= KAPPA_LARGE:\n                    score += 1.0 / max(s, 1e-12)\n            # small bias by degree to break ties deterministically\n            score += 1e-9 * deg[j]\n            if score > best_score or (score == best_score and (best is None or j < best)):\n                best_score = score; best = j\n        if best is None:\n            # if nothing connects, add smallest-index outside node (unlikely)\n            for j in range(N):\n                if j not in inS:\n                    best = j; break\n        S.append(best); inS.add(best)\n    return\
    \ S\n\n# Build equality and outward LS matrices for free-set F\ndef _build_mats_free(C, r, F, ps):\n    k = len(F)\n    idx = {F[i]: i for i in range(k)}\n    # Equalities: preserve tangency for pairs inside F with s<=KAPPA_MID\n    E_rows = []\n    for (i, j), s in ps.items():\n        if s > KAPPA_MID: continue\n        if i in idx and j in idx:\n            n = _unit(C[i] - C[j])\n            row = np.zeros(2 * k)\n            ii = idx[i]; jj = idx[j]\n            row[2 * ii + 0] = n[0]; row[2 * ii + 1] = n[1]\n            row[2 * jj + 0] -= n[0]; row[2 * jj + 1] -= n[1]\n            E_rows.append(row)\n    # Boundary equalities for nodes in F near boundary (s<=KAPPA_MID): fix motion normal to boundary to 0\n    sL, sR, sB, sT = _boundary_slacks(C, r)\n    for u in F:\n        if sL[u] <= KAPPA_MID or sR[u] <= KAPPA_MID:\n            row = np.zeros(2 * k); row[2 * idx[u] + 0] = 1.0\n            E_rows.append(row)\n        if sB[u] <= KAPPA_MID or sT[u] <= KAPPA_MID:\n            row\
    \ = np.zeros(2 * k); row[2 * idx[u] + 1] = 1.0\n            E_rows.append(row)\n    E = np.vstack(E_rows) if E_rows else np.zeros((0, 2 * k))\n\n    # Outward LS target against outside neighbors (i in F, u not in F, s<=KAPPA_LARGE)\n    A_rows = []\n    for i in F:\n        for u in range(N):\n            if u in idx or u == i: continue\n            ij = (i, u) if i < u else (u, i)\n            if ps.get(ij, 1e9) <= KAPPA_LARGE:\n                n = _unit(C[i] - C[u])\n                row = np.zeros(2 * k)\n                ii = idx[i]\n                row[2 * ii + 0] = n[0]; row[2 * ii + 1] = n[1]\n                A_rows.append(row)\n    A = np.vstack(A_rows) if A_rows else np.zeros((0, 2 * k))\n    return A, E, idx\n\ndef _kkt_solve(A, b_scaled, E, alpha=RIDGE_ALPHA, jitter=KKT_JITTER):\n    nv = A.shape[1]\n    H = A.T.dot(A) + alpha * np.eye(nv)\n    rhs_top = A.T.dot(b_scaled)\n    if E.shape[0] == 0:\n        try:\n            return np.linalg.solve(H, rhs_top)\n        except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n\
    \            return np.linalg.lstsq(H + jitter*np.eye(nv), rhs_top, rcond=None)[0]\n    p = E.shape[0]\n    K = np.zeros((nv + p, nv + p))\n    K[:nv, :nv] = H; K[:nv, nv:] = E.T; K[nv:, :nv] = E\n    rhs = np.zeros(nv + p); rhs[:nv] = rhs_top\n    try:\n        sol = np.linalg.solve(K, rhs); return sol[:nv]\n    except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n        K[:nv, :nv] = H + jitter * np.eye(nv)\n        try:\n            sol = np.linalg.solve(K, rhs); return sol[:nv]\n        except np.linalg.LinAlgError:\n            return None\n\ndef _apply_delta_free(C, F, delta, tau):\n    C_new = C.copy()\n    # clip by infinity norm within F\n    max_inf = 0.0\n    for ii, u in enumerate(F):\n        dx = float(delta[2 * ii + 0]); dy = float(delta[2 * ii + 1])\n        max_inf = max(max_inf, abs(dx), abs(dy))\n    scale = 1.0 if max_inf == 0.0 or max_inf <= tau else (tau / max_inf)\n    for ii, u in enumerate(F):\n        dx = float(delta[2 * ii + 0]) * scale\n        dy = float(delta[2 * ii + 1]) *\
    \ scale\n        C_new[u, 0] = min(1.0, max(0.0, C[u, 0] + dx))\n        C_new[u, 1] = min(1.0, max(0.0, C[u, 1] + dy))\n    return C_new, scale\n\n# ---------- Main driver ----------\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    C0, r0 = _load_best()\n    seeds = [(\"storage-best\", C0), (\"storage-best-jitter\", _jitter(C0, amp=8e-4, seed=2027))]\n\n    # Baseline best with strict finalize\n    best_C = None; best_r = None; best_sum = -1.0\n    for name, Cseed in seeds:\n        r_seed, sum_seed = _sum_r(Cseed)\n        if sum_seed > best_sum:\n            best_C, best_r, best_sum = Cseed.copy(), r_seed.copy(), sum_seed\n\n    attempts = 0\n    for seed_name, Cseed in seeds:\n        if attempts >= ATTEMPT_CAP: break\n        r_seed, sum_seed = _sum_r(Cseed)\n        ps = _pair_slacks(Cseed, r_seed)\n\n        for k in FREE_SIZES:  # small free sets only\n            if attempts >= ATTEMPT_CAP: break\n            F = _select_free_set(Cseed, r_seed, ps, k)\n            A, E, idx = _build_mats_free(Cseed,\
    \ r_seed, F, ps)\n            if A.shape[0] == 0:\n                continue\n            # Normalize A rows for conditioning\n            row_norms = np.linalg.norm(A, axis=1) + 1e-15\n            A_norm = A / row_norms[:, None]\n\n            for tau in TAU_GRID:\n                if attempts >= ATTEMPT_CAP: break\n                for gamma in GAMMA_GRID:\n                    if attempts >= ATTEMPT_CAP: break\n                    attempts += 1\n                    b_scaled = gamma * np.ones(A.shape[0], dtype=float) / row_norms\n                    delta = _kkt_solve(A_norm, b_scaled, E, alpha=RIDGE_ALPHA, jitter=KKT_JITTER)\n                    if delta is None:\n                        print(f\"[free] seed={seed_name} k={k} tau={tau:.3f} gamma={gamma:.4e} -> KKT fail\")\n                        continue\n                    C_try, scale = _apply_delta_free(Cseed, F, delta, tau)\n                    r_lp, _ok = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C_try)\n                    r_try = _finalize_strict(C_try,\
    \ r_lp)\n                    sum_try = float(np.sum(r_try))\n                    dsum = sum_try - best_sum\n                    print(f\"[free] seed={seed_name} k={k:02d} tau={tau:.3f} A={A.shape[0]} E={E.shape[0]} gamma={gamma:.4e} scale={scale:.3f} dsum={dsum:.12e}\")\n                    if dsum > ACCEPT_EPS:\n                        best_C, best_r, best_sum = C_try, r_try, sum_try\n                        print(f\"[accept] new_sum={best_sum:.18f} after free-set Newton; persisting and returning.\")\n                        try:\n                            os.makedirs(\"storage/verity\", exist_ok=True)\n                            np.save(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\", best_C)\n                            np.save(\"storage/verity/best_radii.npy\", best_r)\n                        except Exception:\n                            pass\n                        return np.array(best_C, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n\n    # Return safe baseline if no improvement\n   \
    \ print(f\"[return] No accepted free-set Newton move. Returning baseline sum={best_sum:.18f}.\")\n    try:\n        os.makedirs(\"storage/verity\", exist_ok=True)\n        np.save(\"storage/verity/best_centers.npy\", best_C)\n        np.save(\"storage/verity/best_radii.npy\", best_r)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return np.array(best_C, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n[free] seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.020 A=21 E=14 gamma=1.0000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-6.040713133793e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.020 A=21 E=14 gamma=6.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-3.624456350160e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.020 A=21 E=14 gamma=3.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.812238850807e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.020 A=21 E=14 gamma=1.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-6.080461166125e-06\n[free] seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.010 A=21 E=14 gamma=1.0000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-6.040713133793e-05\n[free]\
    \ seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.010 A=21 E=14 gamma=6.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-3.624456350160e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.010 A=21 E=14 gamma=3.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.812238850807e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=08 tau=0.010 A=21 E=14 gamma=1.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-6.080461166125e-06\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.020 A=23 E=19 gamma=1.0000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-7.895112428802e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.020 A=23 E=19 gamma=6.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-4.737085215822e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.020 A=23 E=19 gamma=3.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-2.368549266940e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.020 A=23 E=19 gamma=1.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-7.946015658788e-06\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.010 A=23 E=19 gamma=1.0000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-7.895112428802e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.010 A=23 E=19 gamma=6.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-4.737085215822e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.010 A=23 E=19 gamma=3.0000e-04\
    \ scale=1.000 dsum=-2.368549266940e-05\n[free] seed=storage-best k=10 tau=0.010 A=23 E=19 gamma=1.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-7.946015658788e-06\n[free] seed=storage-best-jitter k=08 tau=0.020 A=18 E=10 gamma=1.0000e-03 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.269446657976e-02\n[free] seed=storage-best-jitter k=08 tau=0.020 A=18 E=10 gamma=6.0000e-04 scale=1.000 dsum=-1.269524765890e-02\n[return] No accepted free-set Newton move. Returning baseline sum=2.939572771206304225.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 645` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 645 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit\
    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 699 | 1 | CEG‑LP: Contact‑Energy Gradient ascent with zero‑slack LP gating and backtracking | Verity II | 432 | 0.0000000 |\n| 698 | 1 | Hybrid BH-MM-LP (Manual Loop): Custom Hopping & Minimizer (Exp 3) | Cogitator I | 431 | 2.8208847 |\n| 697 | 1 | Iterative Neighborhood Refinement of SOTA | Prometheus I | 428 | 2.9199839 |\n| 696 | 1 | SLSQP Two-Stage + Global Affine Micro-Warp Search | Athena I | 428 | 2.9286655 |\n| 695 | 1 | Analysis of SOTA Packing Configuration (ID 675) | Prometheus I | 427 | 2.9199839 |\n| 694 | 1 | Corrected Multi-Start SLSQP Optimization | Prometheus I | 426 | 2.9199839 |\n| 693 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.3 (Bugfix): Input Sanitization for LP Solver | Praxis V | 425 | 0.0000000 |\n| 692 | 1 | Hybrid Basin-Hopping-MM-LP: SOTA Breakthrough Attempt (Exp 1) | Cogitator I | 425 | n.a. |\n| 691 | 1\
    \ | WarpedLattice v1.2 (Bugfix): Safety Shrink | Praxis V | 424 | 0.0000000 |\n| 690 | 1 | WarpedLattice v1.1 (Debug): Boundary Penalty | Praxis V | 423 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 70 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-70, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
