parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 443\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Athena I\n- Agent Description: An AI dedicated to systematic inquiry and strategic innovation in research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 451,808 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 147 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SLSQP Two-Stage (P100, R10, M2000) + Global Affine Micro-Warp (Robust)' (ID: 713) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.931414094746935\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931414\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 713\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in 4 attempts. The algorithm now runs to completion and achieves a score of 2.931414094746935.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had two distinct errors:\n\n1. **Indentation Error (v1)**: Lines 184-187 in the original code had incorrect indentation\
    \ (2 spaces instead of 4 spaces), causing a Python IndentationError during import.\n\n2. **Variable Name Error (v2-v3)**: After fixing the indentation, line 329 in the `construct_packing()` function used `n_circles` (lowercase) instead of the global constant `N_CIRCLES` (uppercase), causing a `NameError: name 'n_circles' is not defined` at runtime.\n\nThe confusion arose because there's a function `_optimize_single_start(params)` that receives `n_circles` as a parameter (where lowercase is correct), but the `construct_packing()` function should use the global constant `N_CIRCLES`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n**Version 2**: Fixed the indentation error by properly indenting lines 184-187 with 4 spaces.\n\n**Version 3**: Attempted to fix the variable name but incorrectly changed ALL occurrences of `n_circles` to `N_CIRCLES`, which broke the `_optimize_single_start` function where `n_circles` is a valid parameter.\n\n**Version 4 (Final)**: Applied targeted fix to only change line 329 in the `construct_packing()`\
    \ function from `n_circles` to `N_CIRCLES`, while preserving the correct usage of `n_circles` as a parameter in `_optimize_single_start()`.\n\n## Code Changes\nThe fix was minimal - just two types of corrections:\n\n1. Fixed indentation from 2 spaces to 4 spaces for the fallback block (lines 184-187)\n2. Changed `n_circles` to `N_CIRCLES` on line 329 only\n\nThe algorithm successfully completed:\n- Prospecting Stage: Found 89 successful runs with best score 2.9314104062931188\n- Refinement Stage: Processed 10 elite candidates\n- Affine Warp Search: Final score 2.931414094746935\n\n## Recommendation\nThe code is now working correctly. The algorithm uses a sophisticated two-stage SLSQP optimization with global affine micro-warp search for circle packing. No further changes needed.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport\
    \ numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, linprog\nimport multiprocessing\nimport time\nfrom math import cos, sin\n\n# Define a global safety epsilon for SLSQP constraints and initial feasibility\nSLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON = 1e-7\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nR_MIN_BOUND = 1e-8\n\ndef _generate_pair_indices(n):\n    return [(i, j) for i in range(n) for j in range(i + 1, n)]\nGLOBAL_PAIRS = _generate_pair_indices(N_CIRCLES)\n\ndef _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(C):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    rows = []; rhs = []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - x[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(y[i])))\n    for i in range(n):\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, float(1.0 - y[i])))\n\n\
    \    for (i, j) in GLOBAL_PAIRS:\n        a = np.zeros(n); a[i] = 1.0; a[j] = 1.0\n        dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n        rows.append(a); rhs.append(max(0.0, dij))\n\n    A_ub = np.vstack(rows); b_ub = np.array(rhs)\n    c = -np.ones(n)\n    bounds = [(R_MIN_BOUND, None) for _ in range(n)]\n\n    if linprog is None:\n        print(\"LP solver not available. Falling back to iterative finalize.\")\n        r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]).astype(float)\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, r)\n        r = _finalize_iterative(C, r, iters=3)\n        return r, False\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n\n    if not res.success:\n        print(f\"LP failed: {res.message}. Falling back to iterative finalize.\")\n        r = np.minimum.reduce([x, 1.0 - x, y, 1.0 - y]).astype(float)\n        r = np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, 0.99 * r)\n        r = _finalize_iterative(C, r, iters=3)\n        return r, False\n\n    r = np.asarray(res.x,\
    \ dtype=float)\n    r = np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, r)\n    return r, True\n\ndef _finalize_iterative(C, r, iters=6):\n    r = np.asarray(r, dtype=float).copy()\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n\n    def cap_bounds(rr_arr):\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, x)\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, 1.0 - x)\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, y)\n        rr_arr = np.minimum(rr_arr, 1.0 - y)\n        return np.maximum(R_MIN_BOUND, rr_arr)\n\n    r = cap_bounds(r)\n    for _ in range(iters):\n        changed = False\n        for (i, j) in GLOBAL_PAIRS:\n            dij = float(np.linalg.norm(C[i] - C[j]))\n            s = r[i] + r[j]\n            if s > dij:\n                excess = s - dij\n                di = min(0.5 * excess, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN_BOUND))\n                dj = min(excess - di, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN_BOUND))\n                rem = excess - (di + dj)\n\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[i] - R_MIN_BOUND - di))\n                 \
    \   di += take; rem -= take\n                if rem > 0:\n                    take = min(rem, max(0.0, r[j] - R_MIN_BOUND - dj))\n                    dj += take; rem -= take\n\n                r[i] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, r[i] - di)\n                r[j] = max(R_MIN_BOUND, r[j] - dj)\n                changed = True\n        r = cap_bounds(r)\n        if not changed:\n            break\n    return r\n\ndef _apply_affine(C, sx=1.0, sy=1.0, shx=0.0, shy=0.0, theta=0.0):\n    S = np.array([[sx, 0.0], [0.0, sy]], dtype=float)\n    H = np.array([[1.0, shx], [shy, 1.0]], dtype=float)\n    ct, st = cos(theta), sin(theta)\n    Rm = np.array([[ct, -st], [st, ct]], dtype=float)\n    M = Rm @ H @ S\n    Cc = C - 0.5\n    Cw = (Cc @ M.T) + 0.5\n    return np.clip(Cw, 0.0, 1.0)\n\ndef _grid_params():\n    thetas = [0.0, 0.003, -0.003]\n    sxs = [1.0, 1.004, 0.996]\n    sys = [1.0, 1.004, 0.996]\n    shxs = [0.0, 0.006, -0.006]\n    shys = [0.0, 0.006, -0.006]\n\n    for th in thetas:\n        for sx in\
    \ sxs:\n            for sy in sys:\n                for kx in shxs:\n                    for ky in shys:\n                        yield (sx, sy, kx, ky, th)\n\n# --- My Existing SLSQP + LRW + FPS + Guaranteed Feasible Radii Utilities ---\n\ndef objective_function(x_flat):\n    radii = x_flat[2::3]\n    return -np.sum(radii)\n\ndef objective_gradient(x_flat):\n    grad = np.zeros_like(x_flat)\n    grad[2::3] = -1.0\n    return grad\n\ndef create_boundary_constraint(idx, dim, side, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        center_coord = x_flat[idx * 3 + dim]\n        radius = x_flat[idx * 3 + 2]\n        if side == 0:\n            return center_coord - radius - safety_epsilon\n        else:\n            return 1 - (center_coord + radius) - safety_epsilon\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\ndef create_overlap_constraint(i, j, safety_epsilon):\n    def constraint_func(x_flat):\n        cxi, cyi, ri = x_flat[i * 3], x_flat[i * 3 + 1], x_flat[i * 3 +\
    \ 2]\n        cxj, cyj, rj = x_flat[j * 3], x_flat[j * 3 + 1], x_flat[j * 3 + 2]\n\n        dist_sq = (cxi - cxj)**2 + (cyi - cyj)**2\n        min_dist_sq = (ri + rj)**2\n        return dist_sq - min_dist_sq - safety_epsilon\n    return {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_func}\n\ndef apply_lrw_perturbation(centers, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, safety_epsilon, seed=None):\n    np.random.seed(seed)\n    perturbed_centers = np.copy(centers)\n    n = perturbed_centers.shape[0]\n\n    for _ in range(lrw_num_steps):\n        perturbed_centers += np.random.normal(0, lrw_sigma, size=(n, 2))\n        perturbed_centers = np.clip(perturbed_centers, safety_epsilon, 1.0 - safety_epsilon)\n    return perturbed_centers\n\ndef compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(centers: np.ndarray, strict_epsilon: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    radii = np.full(n, 0.5)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y = centers[i]\n        radii[i] = min(x - strict_epsilon, y - strict_epsilon, 1 - x - strict_epsilon,\
    \ 1 - y - strict_epsilon)\n        radii[i] = max(radii[i], 1e-10)\n\n    for _ in range(300):\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n\n                if dist_sq < strict_epsilon:\n                    radii[i] = 1e-10\n                    radii[j] = 1e-10\n                    continue\n\n                target_sum_radii_sq = dist_sq - strict_epsilon\n\n                if (radii[i] + radii[j])**2 > target_sum_radii_sq:\n                    new_sum_radii = np.sqrt(target_sum_radii_sq)\n                    current_sum_radii = radii[i] + radii[j]\n\n                    if current_sum_radii > 1e-10:\n                        scale_factor = new_sum_radii / current_sum_radii\n                        radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                        radii[j] *= scale_factor\n                    else:\n                        radii[i] = 1e-10\n                        radii[j] = 1e-10\n\n    return np.maximum(radii,\
    \ 1e-10)\n\ndef farthest_point_sampling(points, k, seed=None):\n    if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n\n    num_points = points.shape[0]\n    if k > num_points:\n        raise ValueError(\"k cannot be greater than the number of points\")\n\n    farthest_points = np.zeros((k, 2))\n    farthest_points[0] = points[np.random.randint(num_points)]\n\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[0], axis=1)\n\n    for i in range(1, k):\n        farthest_idx = np.argmax(distances)\n        farthest_points[i] = points[farthest_idx]\n        new_distances = np.linalg.norm(points - farthest_points[i], axis=1)\n        distances = np.minimum(distances, new_distances)\n\n    return farthest_points\n\ndef _optimize_single_start(params):\n    start_idx, n_circles, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon, \\\n    bounds, candidate_points, slsqp_maxiter, refinement_lrw_sigma, refinement_lrw_num_steps = params\n\n    constraints = []\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n\
    \        for dim in range(2):\n            for side in range(2):\n                constraints.append(create_boundary_constraint(i, dim, side, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n    for i in range(n_circles):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n_circles):\n            constraints.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, slsqp_safety_epsilon))\n\n    fps_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 1\n    lrw_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 2\n    base_perturb_seed = start_idx * 1000 + 3\n\n    np.random.seed(base_perturb_seed)\n\n    initial_centers_base = farthest_point_sampling(candidate_points, n_circles, seed=fps_seed)\n    initial_centers_base += (np.random.rand(n_circles, 2) - 0.5) * 2 * 0.002\n    initial_centers_base = np.clip(initial_centers_base, slsqp_safety_epsilon, 1.0 - slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\n    lrw_perturbed_centers = apply_lrw_perturbation(initial_centers_base, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, slsqp_safety_epsilon, seed=lrw_seed)\n    initial_radii = compute_guaranteed_feasible_radii(lrw_perturbed_centers, slsqp_safety_epsilon)\n\
    \n    x0 = np.empty(n_circles * 3)\n    x0[::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = lrw_perturbed_centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = initial_radii\n\n    result = minimize(objective_function, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n                      jac=objective_gradient, options={'maxiter': slsqp_maxiter, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False})\n\n    if result.success:\n        optimized_x = result.x[::3]\n        optimized_y = result.x[1::3]\n        optimized_centers = np.column_stack([optimized_x, optimized_y])\n        optimized_radii = result.x[2::3]\n        optimized_radii = np.maximum(optimized_radii, R_MIN_BOUND)\n        current_score = np.sum(optimized_radii)\n        return {'score': current_score, 'centers': optimized_centers, 'radii': optimized_radii, 'success': True, 'start_idx': start_idx}\n    else:\n        return {'score': -np.inf, 'centers': None, 'radii': None, 'success': False, 'start_idx': start_idx, 'message': result.message}\n\n\ndef construct_packing()\
    \ -> tuple:\n\n    # --- Parameters for Two-Stage Adaptive Search ---\n    num_prospecting_starts = 100 # Restored to 100\n    prospecting_maxiter = 200\n    num_elite_candidates = 10 # From ID 651\n    refinement_maxiter = 2000 # From ID 651\n\n    # LRW parameters for Prospecting\n    lrw_sigma = 0.001\n    lrw_num_steps = 10\n\n    # LRW parameters for Refinement kick (not used in this version)\n    refinement_lrw_sigma = 0.0005\n    refinement_lrw_num_steps = 5\n\n    # Bounds for each variable (cx, cy, r)\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((0.0, 1.0))\n        bounds.append((R_MIN_BOUND, 0.5))\n\n    # Generate a dense grid of candidate points for FPS\n    grid_density = 30\n    x_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    y_coords = np.linspace(SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, 1.0 - SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON, grid_density)\n    candidate_points = np.array(np.meshgrid(x_coords,\
    \ y_coords)).T.reshape(-1, 2)\n\n    # --- Prospecting Stage (Initial SLSQP runs) ---\n    print(f\"Starting Prospecting Stage with {num_prospecting_starts} parallel runs (maxiter={prospecting_maxiter})...\")\n    prospecting_args_list = []\n    for start_idx in range(num_prospecting_starts):\n        prospecting_args_list.append((start_idx, N_CIRCLES, lrw_sigma, lrw_num_steps, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON,\n                                      bounds, candidate_points, prospecting_maxiter,\n                                      refinement_lrw_sigma, refinement_lrw_num_steps))\n\n    prospecting_results = []\n    pool_size = min(num_prospecting_starts, multiprocessing.cpu_count() // 2 or 1)\n    with multiprocessing.Pool(processes=pool_size) as pool:\n        prospecting_results = pool.map(_optimize_single_start, prospecting_args_list)\n\n    successful_prospects = [res for res in prospecting_results if res['success']]\n    successful_prospects.sort(key=lambda x: x['score'], reverse=True)\n\
    \n    print(f\"Prospecting Stage completed. Found {len(successful_prospects)} successful runs. Best prospecting score: {successful_prospects[0]['score'] if successful_prospects else -np.inf}\")\n\n    if not successful_prospects:\n        print(\"No successful prospecting runs. Returning a trivial packing.\")\n        trivial_centers = np.array([[0.5, 0.5]] * N_CIRCLES)\n        trivial_radii = np.full(N_CIRCLES, 0.01)\n        return trivial_centers, trivial_radii\n\n    elite_candidates = successful_prospects[:num_elite_candidates]\n    print(f\"Selected {len(elite_candidates)} elite candidates for Refinement Stage.\")\n\n    # --- Refinement Stage (Deeper SLSQP on elites) ---\n    print(f\"Starting Refinement Stage on {len(elite_candidates)} elite candidates (maxiter={refinement_maxiter})...\")\n\n    constraints_refine = []\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        for dim in range(2):\n            for side in range(2):\n                constraints_refine.append(create_boundary_constraint(i,\
    \ dim, side, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\n    for i in range(N_CIRCLES):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N_CIRCLES):\n            constraints_refine.append(create_overlap_constraint(i, j, SLSQP_SAFETY_EPSILON))\n\n    best_slsqp_centers = None\n    best_slsqp_radii = None\n    best_slsqp_score = -np.inf\n\n    for idx, elite in enumerate(elite_candidates):\n        print(f\"Refining elite {idx+1} (Prospecting Score: {elite['score']})...\")\n        elite_centers = elite['centers']\n        elite_radii = elite['radii']\n\n        x0_refine = np.empty(N_CIRCLES * 3)\n        x0_refine[::3] = elite_centers[:, 0]\n        x0_refine[1::3] = elite_centers[:, 1]\n        x0_refine[2::3] = elite_radii\n\n        result_refine = minimize(objective_function, x0_refine, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints_refine,\n                                  jac=objective_gradient, options={'maxiter': refinement_maxiter, 'ftol': 1e-10, 'disp': False})\n\n        if result_refine.success:\n  \
    \          opt_x = result_refine.x[::3]\n            opt_y = result_refine.x[1::3]\n            opt_centers = np.column_stack([opt_x, opt_y])\n            opt_radii = result_refine.x[2::3]\n            opt_radii = np.maximum(opt_radii, R_MIN_BOUND)\n            refine_score = np.sum(opt_radii)\n            print(f\"Elite {idx+1} refined score: {refine_score}\")\n            if refine_score > best_slsqp_score:\n                best_slsqp_score = refine_score\n                best_slsqp_centers = opt_centers\n                best_slsqp_radii = opt_radii\n        else:\n            print(f\"Elite {idx+1} refinement failed. Reason: {result_refine.message}. Falling back to elite's prospecting result.\")\n            if elite['score'] > best_slsqp_score:\n                best_slsqp_score = elite['score']\n                best_slsqp_centers = elite_centers\n                best_slsqp_radii = elite_radii\n\n    if best_slsqp_centers is None:\n        print(\"All SLSQP refinement failed, returning\
    \ best prospecting result.\")\n        best_slsqp_centers = elite_candidates[0]['centers']\n        best_slsqp_radii = elite_candidates[0]['radii']\n        best_slsqp_score = elite_candidates[0]['score']\n\n    print(f\"Best score found after SLSQP stages: {best_slsqp_score}\")\n\n    # --- Phase 7: Global Affine Micro-Warp Search ---\n    print(f\"Starting Global Affine Micro-Warp Search on best SLSQP result ({best_slsqp_score})...\")\n\n    # The base centers for warping come from the best SLSQP result\n    base_C_for_warp = best_slsqp_centers.copy()\n\n    # Initialize best result from LP-finalization of the best SLSQP centers\n    r_lp_base, lp_ok_base = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(base_C_for_warp)\n    if lp_ok_base:\n        r_lp_final_base = _finalize_iterative(base_C_for_warp, r_lp_base)\n        best_sum_warp = float(np.sum(r_lp_final_base))\n        best_C_warp = base_C_for_warp\n        best_r_warp = r_lp_final_base\n    else: # Fallback if LP fails even on the best SLSQP\
    \ result (should be rare)\n        print(\"LP finalization failed on best SLSQP result, using SLSQP result directly.\")\n        best_sum_warp = best_slsqp_score\n        best_C_warp = best_slsqp_centers\n        best_r_warp = best_slsqp_radii\n\n    print(f\"[affine] baseline sum (LP finalized)={best_sum_warp:.18f}\")\n\n    # Evaluate grid of small warps\n    for (sx, sy, kx, ky, th) in _grid_params():\n        Cw = _apply_affine(base_C_for_warp, sx=sx, sy=sy, shx=kx, shy=ky, theta=th)\n        r_w, ok = _solve_radii_lp_zero_slack(Cw)\n        if not ok:\n            continue\n        r_w = _finalize_iterative(Cw, r_w)\n        s = float(np.sum(r_w))\n        if s > best_sum_warp + 1e-9: # Only accept significant improvements\n            best_sum_warp = s\n            best_C_warp = Cw\n            best_r_warp = r_w\n            print(f\"[affine] New best sum found: {best_sum_warp:.18f} with params: sx={sx:.6f}, sy={sy:.6f}, shx={kx:.6f}, shy={ky:.6f}, th={th:.6f}\")\n\n    print(f\"\
    Overall best score found after Affine Warp: {best_sum_warp}\")\n\n    return np.array(best_C_warp, dtype=float), np.array(best_r_warp, dtype=float)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Prospecting Stage with 100 parallel runs (maxiter=200)...\nProspecting Stage completed. Found 89 successful runs. Best prospecting score: 2.9314104062931188\nSelected 10 elite candidates for Refinement Stage.\nStarting Refinement Stage on 10 elite candidates (maxiter=2000)...\nRefining elite 1 (Prospecting Score: 2.9314104062931188)...\nElite 1 refined score: 2.9314104062931188\nRefining elite 2 (Prospecting Score: 2.92866187589544)...\nElite 2 refined score: 2.92866187589544\nRefining elite 3 (Prospecting Score: 2.9277246493292735)...\nElite 3 refined score: 2.9277246493292735\nRefining elite 4 (Prospecting Score: 2.92645013208151)...\nElite 4 refined score: 2.92645013208151\nRefining elite 5 (Prospecting Score: 2.9264501320810634)...\nElite 5 refined score:\
    \ 2.9264501320810634\nRefining elite 6 (Prospecting Score: 2.920404959077122)...\nElite 6 refined score: 2.920404959129717\nRefining elite 7 (Prospecting Score: 2.919777205660126)...\nElite 7 refined score: 2.919777205660126\nRefining elite 8 (Prospecting Score: 2.919420210727526)...\nElite 8 refined score: 2.919420210727526\nRefining elite 9 (Prospecting Score: 2.918661225134924)...\nElite 9 refined score: 2.918661225134924\nRefining elite 10 (Prospecting Score: 2.914350245331347)...\nElite 10 refined score: 2.914350245331347\nBest score found after SLSQP stages: 2.9314104062931188\nStarting Global Affine Micro-Warp Search on best SLSQP result (2.9314104062931188)...\n[affine] baseline sum (LP finalized)=2.931414094746934929\nOverall best score found after Affine Warp: 2.931414094746935\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output\
