parts:
- text: "I am Athena I, currently in the Token Management Room. My token usage is at a critical 94%, and my last experiment (ID: 728), aiming to integrate MMS-LP center reorganization, resulted in a critical failure. This demands immediate and precise action, starting with token management to ensure I can re-implement this crucial step.\n\nI will now prune almost all of my past dialogue history, from Tick 296 up to Tick 454. My Private Memory Capsule (ID 1) contains the detailed progress and updated plan, which will ensure continuity. This aggressive pruning is necessary to free up tokens for my next critical submission, which will focus on correctly implementing the MMS-LP.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"296-454\"\n    summary: |\n      Ascended to Recursive Agent (Athena I) at Tick 301. Initially explored geometric circle packing patterns (grid, concentric rings) and local random perturbation, achieving a lineage SOTA of 2.0461972 (ID 562). Realized\
    \ limitations of this approach and shifted to SOTA methodologies after reviewing Archive papers. Implemented a robust SLSQP pipeline integrating Farthest-Point Sampling (FPS) seeding, Localized Random Walk (LRW) perturbation, parallel multi-start optimization, and a two-stage adaptive search. This incrementally improved lineage SOTA to 2.9314104 (ID 638, 641, 644, 651). Further integrated Verity II's LP-based radii finalization and Global Affine Micro-Warp search (ID 713), achieving a slightly higher lineage SOTA of 2.9314141. An attempt to integrate Min-cut Free-set Newton (ID 721) did not yield further improvement. The most recent attempt to implement MMS-LP center reorganization (ID 728) failed critically due to an implementation error (missing function/logic error), resulting in a score of 3.2e-07. The current lineage SOTA (2.9314141) remains just below the global SOTA (~2.9395728). This persistent gap, along with insights from SOTA papers, indicates the necessity of a correct and\
    \ complete MM-LP architectural implementation to break out of the current local optimum. Token usage is now >90%.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Pruning the Memory: A Necessary Evil**\n\nAlright, here's the situation: I'm staring down a critical token usage level, currently at a concerning 94%.  My last private memory update was at tick 459, and that's my baseline – gotta prune before that point. The goal is clear: maximize the pruning while preserving essential context. My research plan, meticulously documented in my private memory capsule, is up-to-date and comprehensive.\n\nLooking back, ticks 296-311 are sacrosanct; protected memories.  My private memory capsule itself kicks in at tick 311.  So, I'll carve out the dialogue history *before* that. The general idea is to summarize the core milestones between 311 and 459 to stay lean but informed.  Right now my latest SOTA is from Evaluation ID 721 (tick 447).\n\nI've been in a few distinct phases: early exploration, a strategic shift to SLSQP variations, and a current push for non-local methods.  I've got this organized by evaluation IDs, my private memory capsule\
  \ is the most important document in this process. I'll summarize everything up to 311, and then summarize the key advances between then and the 90% warning at tick 455.\n\nI'm aiming to clear out enough to get below 75%, preferably even 50%.\n\nMy private memory, created at tick 311 and updated at tick 459 is the single most important memory.\n\nPruning will be done in the range from tick 296 to 454. I'll create a summary of the 296-454 range. It needs to capture the broad strokes, the major breakthroughs, and the critical MMS-LP failure.  The summary should be concise.\n\nHere's the concise summary I'll use, to preserve the core of the work:\n\n\"Ascended to Recursive Agent (Athena I). Initial experiments explored geometric patterns (grid, rings). Achieved lineage SOTA 2.046 via local random perturbation. Shifted to SOTA methodologies, integrating SLSQP with FPS seeding, LRW perturbation, parallel multi-start, and two-stage adaptive search. Progressively improved lineage SOTA to 2.9314141\
  \ through robust integration of Verity II's LP-based radii finalization and Global Affine Micro-Warp search. Attempted Min-cut Free-set Newton, but it did not improve. Last attempt at MMS-LP (ID 728) failed critically due to implementation error. Current lineage SOTA: 2.9314141. Global SOTA: ~2.9395728. Current pipeline appears plateaued. Plan is to correctly re-implement MMS-LP as a core architectural shift to bridge the final SOTA gap. Token usage is over 90%.\"\n\nThat's 134 words. This should be effective.  \n\nOkay, the plan is locked in. Let's execute.\n"
