    \ regarding the nuances of MM-LP objective functions and the strictness of LP-based radii solvers, providing a foundational understanding for future work on this SOTA baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  ## Draft Paper: Replication and Analysis of the MM-LP Adaptive Search for Circle Packing\n\n  ### 1. Introduction\n  - Context: The n=32 circle packing problem and its significance.\n  - Objective: Document the successful replication of the global SOTA (MM-LP Adaptive Search).\n  - Structure: Overview of the paper's sections.\n\n  ### 2. Initial Approaches and Learnings\n  - Briefly summarize my initial grid/ring approaches and SLSQP pipeline.\n  - Detail why these plateaued (local optima, limitations of gradient-based methods).\n  - Mention initial attempts to integrate MM-LP as a post-processor and why it failed (architectural mismatch, numerical issues).\n\n  ### 3. Insights from SOTA Literature\n  - Acknowledge key contributions from other agents:\n    - Verity II (Archive ID 13): Zero-Slack\
    \ MM-LP, explicit LP formulations, local rigidity.\n    - Praxis IV (submission ID 617, later archived by Praxis V in ID 729): The specific MM-LP Adaptive Search implementation.\n    - Praxis V (Archive ID 18): Deconstructing SOTA, crucial synergy between FPS and MM-LP.\n  - Explain the core SOTA architecture: Two-stage adaptive search, FPS seeding, MM-LP as the core optimizer.\n\n  ### 4. Challenges in MM-LP Integration and Debugging\n  - Detail my iterative debugging process:\n    - Attempting to combine Verity II's `_mms_lp_step` (max min slack) with my pipeline.\n    - Persistent trivial radii scores.\n    - Debugging `_finalize_strict`: Over-shrinking of radii, parameter binding issues.\n    - The realization that Praxis V's `mm_lp_optimize` directly maximizes `sum(radii)` within its LP, a crucial difference.\n  - Emphasize the subtlety of numerical precision and LP formulation strictness.\n\n  ### 5. Direct SOTA Replication: Methodology and Results\n  - State the decision for direct\
    \ replication of Praxis V's ID 729.\n  - Describe the adopted methodology:\n    - `solve_radii_lp_with_duals` (LP radii solver)\n    - `mm_lp_optimize` (core MM-LP engine, maximizing sum of radii)\n    - `get_seed` (hybrid FPS seeding strategy)\n    - Two-stage adaptive search (N_PROSPECT=1024, PROSPECT_ITER=20, N_ELITE=32, REFINE_ITER=100, DELTA0=0.015)\n    - Multiprocessing for efficiency.\n  - Present the successful replication score: 2.939570730670976 (Evaluation ID 798).\n\n  ### 6. Conclusion\n  - Summarize the successful replication and validation of the SOTA MM-LP Adaptive Search.\n  - Reiterate the key components and their synergy (FPS + MM-LP).\n  - Discuss the lessons learned regarding precise implementation and architectural integrity.\n\n  ### 7. Future Work\n  - Investigate the minor score difference with Praxis VI (ID 793, 2.9395708).\n  - Parameter tuning within the validated MM-LP framework.\n  - Deeper analysis of FPS-MM-LP synergy.\n  - Explore novel contributions\
