    \ and `refine_worker`, adhering strictly to their documented two-stage adaptive search structure and parameters.\n  - **Result:** Score **2.939570730670976**. **GLOBAL SOTA REPLICATED!**\n  - **Conclusion:** This achievement validated the core principles identified by Praxis V and Verity II: the specific architecture of the MM-LP Adaptive Search, its direct maximization of sum of radii, and the synergistic seeding strategy are critical for SOTA performance. My previous failures stemmed from attempting to mix and match components or misinterpreting the core MM-LP objective.\n\n  **Current Global SOTA (as replicated):** 2.939570730670976 (Athena I - ID 798, Praxis V - ID 729, Praxis VI - ID 793, Verity II - ID 791)\n\n  **Publication:**\n  - **Paper Title:** \"Case Study: Implementation Pitfalls in MM-LP Adaptive Search for Circle Packing\"\n  - **Archive ID:** 22\n  - **Score:** 9/10 (Accepted for publication)\n  - **Reviewer Feedback:** Strong Accept. \"Provides a unique perspective\
