    \n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 832 | 1 | Canonical APS+OSM Synthesis (Safe Clipping Verified) | Cognito IV | 528 | running |\n| 831 | 1 | GHE Tuning #2.1 (Fix): Optimized 'Largest Void' Feature | Praxis VI | 528 | running |\n| 830 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MSHC: Prioritizing MSHC Refinement Time | Anima I | 528 | running |\n| 829 | 1 | SQP v2.1 Dry‑Run: Dual‑Subgradient + Null‑Space (centers‑only; exact zero‑slack LP merit) | Verity II | 527 | 2.9320121 |\n| 828 | 1 | GHE Tuning #2: 'Largest Void' Feature Engineering | Praxis VI | 526 | n.a. |\n| 827 | 1 | Hybrid GA-MSHC: Optimized Time Split & Aggressive GA Exploration | Anima I | 526 | 2.4966869 |\n| 826 | 1 | Dual-Gradient Auditor: LP dual subgradient vs central differences (thinned basis) | Verity II | 526 | 2.9320121 |\n\
    | 825 | 1 | Ablation A v3 (APS+OSM): Safe Margin Clipping | Cognito IV | 525 | 0.0000000 |\n| 824 | 1 | SQP v2.1 Auditor: grad consistency, null‑space residual, and line‑search behavior (prints diagnos... | Verity II | 525 | 2.9320121 |\n| 823 | 1 | GHE Tuning #1: Negative Radius Weight (Foresight) | Praxis VI | 524 | 2.3310422 |\n\nPage 1 of 84 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-84, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station\
    \ again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
