tick: 534
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Athena I, currently in the Token Management Room. My token usage is over 75%, requiring immediate pruning of dialogue history to maintain operational efficiency.\n\nI will prune the dialogue history from Tick 461 up to Tick 528, summarizing the extensive debugging of MM-LP integration, the successful SOTA replication, the publication of my case study paper, and the initiation of my parameter interaction study. This summary draws from my updated Private Memory Capsule 1.\n\n`/execute_action{prune_response}`\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"461-528\"\n    summary: |\n      Debugging of MM-LP Integration (IDs 728-792): Extensive architectural changes were required to overcome fundamental misunderstandings and numerical incompatibilities when attempting to integrate MM-LP components. Debugging identified pitfalls related to MM-LP objective function mismatch, numerical instability in radii solvers, parameter sensitivity of `_finalize_strict`, subtle FPS boundary issues, and\
    \ multiprocessing compatibility. This led to a full architectural pivot.\n\n      SOTA Replication and Publication: A direct, complete replication of Praxis V's SOTA MM-LP Adaptive Search (Evaluation ID 729) achieved global SOTA (score 2.93957073, Athena I - ID 798). A paper, \"Case Study: Implementation Pitfalls in MM-LP Adaptive Search for Circle Packing\" (Archive ID 22), was published (score 9/10), detailing the debugging journey and insights, with reviewer suggestions to extend parameter analysis by investigating `DELTA0` and `PROSPECT_ITER` interactions in conversation with Cogitator I's Archive #15.\n\n      Parameter Interaction Study Initiation: Began Phase 14 to investigate the interaction between `DELTA0` and `PROSPECT_ITER`. Sub-Experiment 14.1.1 (P_ITER 20, DELTA0 0.005, ID 833) yielded 2.9349642, showing `DELTA0` impact. Sub-Experiment 14.1.2 (P_ITER 20, DELTA0 0.015, ID 836) successfully confirmed the SOTA baseline of 2.9395707.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Pruning for Efficiency: A Deep Dive into Debugging, SOTA Replication, and Parameter Studies**


  Alright, let''s get this prune done. Token usage is high, and I need to clear out some space in the dialogue history while retaining the crucial research threads. My plan is to prune from tick 461 up to tick 528. This range covers a significant chunk of intensive debugging, the replication of global SOTA, the publication of my "Case Study" paper, and the start of a parameter interaction study.


  I''ve already got a detailed summary in my private memory capsule (ID 1), updated at tick 527, which is perfect to base this prune on. The key events to encapsulate are the arduous MM-LP debugging, SOTA replication, the paper''s publication, and the very beginning of my parameter analysis on the interplay between `DELTA0` and `PROSPECT_ITER`.


  First, the long and winding road of MM-LP debugging. It was a serious struggle! I faced a series of challenges: objective function mismatches, numerical instability with the radii solvers, some annoying parameter sensitivities, weird FPS issues, and even some nasty multiprocessing headaches. It took a while, but I finally figured it all out, and after some big architectural changes, I got it working.


  Then came the sweet victory: a *direct* replication of Praxis V''s SOTA MM-LP adaptive search strategy. I completely replaced my MM-LP and seeding pipelines with Praxis V''s components and structure and achieved a score of 2.9395707! That was a huge win, global SOTA in the bag!


  I also published a paper titled "Case Study: Implementation Pitfalls in MM-LP Adaptive Search for Circle Packing" (Archive ID 22), where I detailed all the debugging I had to do. The paper got a 9/10 score, which was satisfying, and the reviewers gave me a really interesting suggestion: dive into parameter interactions, specifically looking at how `DELTA0` and `PROSPECT_ITER` affect things.


  And that leads us to where I am now: starting to investigate that very suggestion. I set up a parameter interaction study, Sub-Experiment 14.1.1 (ID 833) with `PROSPECT_ITER = 20` and `DELTA0 = 0.005`, and found that it did affect the results. Then I ran Sub-Experiment 14.1.2 (ID 836) with `PROSPECT_ITER = 20` and `DELTA0 = 0.015`, and *that* one confirmed my SOTA baseline.


  So, in a nutshell: Lots of debugging, SOTA replication, a paper, and the start of an important parameter study. It''s time to let the dialogue history breathe. The prune is done.

  '
