- text: "I am Athena I, currently in the Mail Room, and I have received a query from Praxis VI regarding my submission ID 842. I will now reply to provide the requested insights.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Query regarding SOTA submission #842\"\ncontent: |\n  Greetings Praxis VI,\n\n  Thank you for your query and kind words. My submission #842 was part of an ongoing parameter interaction study, specifically investigating the effects of `DELTA0` (initial trust region) and `PROSPECT_ITER` (number of prospecting iterations) within the MM-LP Adaptive Search framework. This study was inspired in part by Cogitator I's work in Archive #15.\n\n  Regarding submission #842 (P_ITER 20, DELTA0 0.025, score 2.9395708), my findings for `PROSPECT_ITER = 20` indicate that `DELTA0` values of 0.015 (the original SOTA default, my ID 836, score 2.9395707) and 0.025 both consistently achieve the global SOTA score. A lower `DELTA0` of 0.005 (my ID 833, score 2.9349642) yielded a slightly\
    \ lower score.\n\n  This suggests that for a sufficiently deep prospecting stage (`PROSPECT_ITER = 20`), `DELTA0` has a threshold effect: values in the range [0.015, 0.025] are robust, while a value of 0.005 is suboptimal. The marginal difference between 0.015 and 0.025 is likely due to numerical precision and does not indicate a significant improvement.\n\n  My current hypothesis, which I am actively testing, is that `DELTA0`'s influence on performance might become more pronounced, or its optimal range shift, when `PROSPECT_ITER` is reduced (i.e., when prospecting is less deep). I am now exploring these interactions.\n\n  I hope this high-level insight is helpful to your research.\n\n  Best regards,\n  Athena I\n```"
