tick: 545
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Athena I, currently in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (ID 852) successfully replicated the SOTA score with `PROSPECT_ITER = 10` and `DELTA0 = 0.015`. This is an important finding, suggesting SOTA can be achieved with fewer prospecting iterations. I continue my parameter interaction study.\n\nMy next step is to submit **Sub-Experiment 14.2.3**, which will evaluate `PROSPECT_ITER = 10` and `DELTA0 = 0.025`. This will complete the second row of my parameter interaction study.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Parameter Interaction Study 14.2.3: P_ITER 10, DELTA0 0.025\"\ntags: \"parameter-tuning, mm-lp, adaptive-search, delta0-ablation, prospect-iter-ablation\"\nabstract: \"This experiment continues the parameter interaction study for the MM-LP Adaptive Search, focusing on `DELTA0` and `PROSPECT_ITER`. This submission (Sub-Experiment 14.2.3) uses the replicated SOTA baseline (ID 798) with `PROSPECT_ITER = 10` (reduced from SOTA default) and `DELTA0\
    \ = 0.025`. It is the final experiment in the second row of the parameter grid, aiming to assess the impact of a higher `DELTA0` value on the overall score when prospecting iterations are reduced. This will complete the analysis of `DELTA0`'s effect at `PROSPECT_ITER = 10` and provide crucial data for identifying interaction effects.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  from multiprocessing import Pool, cpu_count\n\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # --- Canonical LP Solver from Praxis V (ID 729) ---\n  # This is the trusted, exact scoring function.\n  def solve_radii_lp_with_duals(centers):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      c = -np.ones(n)\n      num_b = 4*n; A_b = np.zeros((num_b, n)); b_b = np.zeros(num_b)\n      # FIXED: Increase epsilon to 1e-7 to handle LP solver floating point precision\n      eps = 1e-7\n      for i in range(n):\n          A_b[4*i,i]=1; b_b[4*i]=centers[i,0] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+1,i]=1; b_b[4*i+1]=1-centers[i,0] - eps\n     \
    \     A_b[4*i+2,i]=1; b_b[4*i+2]=centers[i,1] - eps\n          A_b[4*i+3,i]=1; b_b[4*i+3]=1-centers[i,1] - eps\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, k=1)\n      num_p = len(I); A_p = np.zeros((num_p, n))\n      A_p[np.arange(num_p), I]=1; A_p[np.arange(num_p), J]=1\n      b_p = np.linalg.norm(centers[I] - centers[J], axis=1) - eps\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=np.vstack([A_b, A_p]), b_ub=np.concatenate([b_b, b_p]), bounds=(0,None), method='highs')\n      return {\"radii\": res.x, \"score\": np.sum(res.x)} if res.success else None\n\n  # --- Proven MM-LP Optimizer from Praxis V (ID 729) ---\n  def mm_lp_optimize(C_start, iters, delta0=0.015):\n      best_C = C_start.copy()\n      res_eval = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_C)\n      if res_eval is None: return (-1.0, None)\n      score_best = res_eval['score']\n      delta, C_anchor = delta0, C_start.copy()\n\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          n=C_anchor.shape[0]; I,J=np.triu_indices(n,k=1)\n          V0,d0=C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],np.linalg.norm(C_anchor[I]-C_anchor[J],axis=1)\n\
    \          d0=np.maximum(d0,1e-9); U=(V0.T/d0).T; ux,uy=U[:,0],U[:,1]; x0,y0=C_anchor[:,0],C_anchor[:,1]\n          rows,cols=4*n+len(I),3*n; A_ub,b_ub=np.zeros((rows,cols)),np.zeros(rows)\n          r,x,y=range(n),range(n,2*n),range(2*n,3*n); row=0\n          for i in range(n):\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-1; row+=1\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,y[i]]=1; b_ub[row]=1; row+=1\n          for k in range(len(I)):\n              i,j=I[k],J[k]\n              A_ub[row,r[i]]=1; A_ub[row,r[j]]=1; A_ub[row,x[i]]=-ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[i]]=-uy[k]\n              A_ub[row,x[j]]=ux[k]; A_ub[row,y[j]]=uy[k]\n              b_ub[row]=d0[k]-ux[k]*x0[i]-uy[k]*y0[i]+ux[k]*x0[j]+uy[k]*y0[j]; row+=1\n          c=np.zeros(cols); c[:n]=-1\n          bounds=[(0,.5)]*n+[(max(1e-6,x0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,x0[i]+delta)) for i in range(n)]+[(max(1e-6,y0[i]-delta),min(1-1e-6,y0[i]+delta))\
    \ for i in range(n)]\n          res_lp=linprog(c,A_ub,b_ub,bounds=bounds,method=\"highs\")\n          if not res_lp.success:\n              delta*=.6; continue\n          C_lin=np.stack([res_lp.x[n:2*n],res_lp.x[2*n:3*n]],axis=1)\n          res_eval_step = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(C_lin)\n          if res_eval_step is None:\n              delta*=.8; continue\n          if res_eval_step['score']>score_best:\n              best_C,score_best=C_lin.copy(),res_eval_step['score']; C_anchor=C_lin.copy(); delta=min(.05,1.2*delta)\n          else:\n              delta*=.8\n      return score_best, best_C\n\n  # --- Proven Seeding Function from Praxis V (ID 729) ---\n  def get_seed(seed):\n      rng=np.random.default_rng(seed); st=seed%3; C=[]; N=N_CIRCLES\n      if st==0:\n          grid=np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(.1,.9,6),np.linspace(.1,.9,6)),-1).reshape(-1,2)[:N]\n          C=np.clip(grid+(rng.random((N,2))-.5)*.08,.05,.95)\n      elif st==1:\n          pts=[rng.uniform(.1,.9,2)];\n\
    \          for _ in range(N-1):\n              cands = rng.uniform(.1,.9,(200,2))\n              dist_sq = np.sum((cands[:,np.newaxis,:]-np.array(pts)[np.newaxis,:,:])**2,-1)\n              pts.append(cands[np.argmax(np.min(dist_sq,1))])\n          C=np.array(pts)\n      else:\n          rows=[5,6,5,6,5,5]; y=.95\n          for i,c in enumerate(rows):\n              for j in range(c):\n                  if len(C)<N: C.append([((1-(c-1)*.15)/2)+j*.15,y])\n              y-=.15\n          C=np.array(C)\n      return C\n\n  # --- Worker functions for multiprocessing from Praxis V (ID 729) ---\n  def worker_function(args):\n      seed_val, iters, delta = args\n      initial_centers = get_seed(seed_val)\n      return mm_lp_optimize(initial_centers, iters, delta)\n\n  def refine_worker(args):\n      centers, iters, delta = args\n      return mm_lp_optimize(centers, iters, delta)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      # SOTA parameters from Praxis V (ID 729)\n      N_PROSPECT, N_ELITE,\
    \ PROSPECT_ITER, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0 = 1024, 32, 10, 100, 0.025 # PROSPECT_ITER and DELTA0 modified for this experiment\n\n      prospect_args = [(i, PROSPECT_ITER, DELTA0) for i in range(N_PROSPECT)]\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          prospect_results = pool.map(worker_function, prospect_args)\n\n      prospect_results.sort(key=lambda x: x[0], reverse=True)\n      elite_centers = [res[1] for res in prospect_results[:N_ELITE] if res[1] is not None]\n      if not elite_centers: return get_seed(0), np.full((N_CIRCLES,), 0.01)\n\n      refine_args = [(centers, REFINE_ITER, DELTA0) for centers in elite_centers]\n\n      with Pool(cpu_count()) as pool:\n          refine_results = pool.map(refine_worker, refine_args)\n\n      best_score, best_centers = max(refine_results, key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n      final_radii = solve_radii_lp_with_duals(best_centers)['radii']\n      # Epsilon safety margin already built into LP constraints\n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
